{
  "program": "COUSR01C",
  "caseId": "case12",
  "description": "The complete eighty-byte record image, stated in full, from five values that are all shorter than the fields they land in. app/cpy/CSUSR01Y.cpy declares SEC-USR-ID X(08) + SEC-USR-FNAME X(20) + SEC-USR-LNAME X(20) + SEC-USR-PWD X(08) + SEC-USR-TYPE X(01) + SEC-USR-FILLER X(23), and the sum of those six spans is the eighty that EXEC CICS WRITE sends at :243 as LENGTH OF SEC-USER-DATA. Every short value is padded on the RIGHT, which is the direction COBOL pads an alphanumeric receiver. SEC-USR-FILLER is assigned by nothing in this program and must still be present and space-filled: drop it and the record is fifty-seven bytes, which is precisely the width the fixture deviation would disguise. The confirmation reads 'User AB has been added ...' with no padding gap, because :256 contributes SEC-USR-ID DELIMITED BY SPACE and the operand stops at the first space of 'AB      '. Concatenating the padded field instead - the classic defect at this site - would read 'User AB       has been added ...'. 'AB      ' also sorts ahead of ADMIN001, so the added row is row zero of the final state.",
